[00:26.94] A whole world is mourning
[00:30.37] For the loss of their king
[00:33.77] In sorrow a new day dawning
[00:36.69] Now the princess is their everything
[00:39.94] A procession to the chambers
[00:43.34] Where they kiss their father's ring
[00:46.48] Can you hear the angel of sadness sing
[00:52.16] With broken wings?
[00:59.24] 
[02:09.03] And with death came disorder
[02:11.67] Who were they now to obey?
[02:14.42] No leader, no followers, no trust, no faith
[02:19.27] The princess is too young to tame a land
[02:22.31] A new king must be chosen
[02:24.77] In search of such a man of trust, there will be contradictions
[02:29.94] 
[02:38.74] Coming forth on desert ground
[02:41.86] The incarnation of a king in sleep profound
[02:45.99] 
[03:05.26] Another self-proclaimed king
[03:09.41] Set to rule in the new empire
[03:13.60] On a mission to save the forsaken ones
[03:17.53] And to re-light the dying fire
[03:26.12] The crowd was confused and divided in two
[03:28.28] A battle was about to begin
[03:30.03] Another man with a will as strong declared a war to win
[03:34.03] His army of believers was faithful, mighty and brave
[03:37.74] Set to capture the liar, to forever enslave
[03:41.70] 
[04:22.83] His troops were marching
[04:27.10] Onto the battlefield
[04:31.50] To set this world on fire
[04:36.70] His forces are never giving yield
[04:42.17] 